      "import os imports Python’s operating-system tools. The variable file_path stores the relative path to important_data.txt. Because it is relative, Python checks for the file in the program’s current working directory.\n",
      "\n",
      "os.path.exists(file_path) checks whether the specified path exists. It returns True if the file or directory is found and False if it does not exist or is an invalid or broken path.\n",
      "\n",
      "The if statement uses this Boolean result to choose which message to display. If the path exists, the first print() runs; otherwise, the else block runs. Each message uses an f-string, allowing the value of file_path to be inserted directly into the output.\n"
     ]
    }
   ],
   "source": [
    "fp = open(absolute_path, 'r')\n",
    "\n",
    "# read file\n",
    "print(fp.read())\n",
    "\n",
    "# Closing the file after reading\n",
    "fp.close()"
   ]
